 \label{thm:large-sieve-general}
Let $\varepsilon > 0$, $X > 0$, $N \ge 1/2$, and $(a_n)_{n \sim N}$ be a complex sequence. Let $q \in \mathbb{Z}_+$, $\mathfrak{a}$ be a cusp of $\Gamma_0(q)$ with $\mu(\mathfrak{a}) = q^{-1}$, and $\sigma_{\mathfrak{a}} \in \textnormal{PSL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ be a scaling matrix for $\mathfrak{a}$. Consider an orthonormal basis of Maass cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(q)$, with eigenvalues $\lambda_j$ and Fourier coefficients $\rho_{j\mathfrak{a}}(n)$ around the cusp $\mathfrak{a}$ (via $\sigma_{\mathfrak{a}}$). Then with $\theta_j := \sqrt{1 - 4\lambda_j}$, one has 
\begin{equation} \label{eq:large-sieve-general}
    \sum_{\lambda_j < 1/4}
    X^{\theta_j} 
    \left\vert 
    \sum_{n \sim N} a_n\, \rho_{j\mathfrak{a}}(n)
    \right\vert^2 
    \ll_\varepsilon 
    (qN)^\varepsilon
    \left(1 + \frac{N}{q}\right) \|a_n\|_2^2,
\end{equation}
for any
\begin{equation} \label{eq:basic-X-range}
    X \ll \max\left(1, \frac{q}{N}, \frac{q^2}{N^3}\right).
\end{equation}

