Let $\varepsilon, X > 0$, $N \ge 1/2$, $\alpha \in \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}$, and $q, a \in \mathbb{Z}_+$. Then with the notation of \cref{thm:large-sieve-general} and the choice of scaling matrix in \cref{eq:scaling-choices}, the bound
